# .worktreeinclude — the gitignored files a fresh git worktree of this repo needs.
# Claude Code reads it when it creates a worktree, and so does any tool that
# honours the same convention. A pattern copies a file only when it matches AND
# is gitignored, so nothing tracked is ever duplicated. A pattern with no slash,
# or one opening with **/, matches at any depth, which is what reaches each
# template's own files.
.env
.env.local
**/.claude/settings.local.json
